Kompakt: Auto's moving phase no longer flashes black and white

Auto enters its fast phase with a manual GL16 to A2 switch, and meink's
state machine answers every manual switch from a 16-grey waveform to a
two-level one with a black clear, a white clear and a redraw: a flash at
the start of every scroll burst. meink keeps a one-shot flag on its
render object, set after energy saving, that makes the next such switch
skip the clear. The loader sets that flag just before the A2 switch of
the moving phase. The settle (A2 to GL16) never flashed. The Kompakt
app's own Text or Quality to Fast switches are unchanged.

--- a/drivers/misc/mudita/eink_loader/loader.c
+++ b/drivers/misc/mudita/eink_loader/loader.c
@@ -43,6 +43,9 @@
  * not know it, so the read-back keeps the old mode. See docs/E-inkdriver.md.
  */
 #define KOMPAKT_AUTO_NAME "KAUTO"
+/* Kompakt: meink's render object ([1] of the Meink handle) and its one-shot "skip the switch clear" flag. */
+#define KOMPAKT_MEINK_RENDER     0x8
+#define KOMPAKT_RENDER_SKIP_CLEAR 0x244
 
 extern void eink_auto_enable(int on, void (*apply)(int moving));
 extern int  eink_auto_state(void);
@@ -152,6 +155,11 @@
         return;
 
     if (moving) {
+        u8 *render = *(u8 **)((u8 *)g_einkData.einkDrv + KOMPAKT_MEINK_RENDER);
+
+        /* Kompakt: a manual GL16 to A2 switch clears black then white first; meink skips that once when this is set. */
+        if (render)
+            WRITE_ONCE(*(u32 *)(render + KOMPAKT_RENDER_SKIP_CLEAR), 1);
         EinkSetWaveformType(g_einkData.einkDrv, kEinkWaveformA2);
         EinkSetBpp(g_einkData.einkDrv, 1);
         EinkSetDitheringParameter(g_einkData.einkDrv, 160);
